        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access permitted. Please use the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a viewing.\r\n\r\nA West Cork Cottage in a blissfully serene setting in mature gardens of 0.8 of an acre which have an abundance of local flora and fauna and impressive views down on to Bantry Bay to the front and to the rear aspect views of Hungry Hill. In the gardens is a cut stone two story famine cottage which needs renovation but has endless possibilities such as guest accommodation or granny flat or staff accommodation. There is also a cut stone ruin.\r\n\r\nThe house dates to the 1920's and has been in the same family since. Numerous original features remain. Rooms have impressive high ceilings which gives a tremendous light and a very airy feel. The house needs a little TLC but has had a replacement roof. With some upcycling and imagination, the property could easily be brought back to its former glory.\r\n\r\nSelf-sufficiency could easily be achieved with the fertile grounds that surround the house. Across from the house is slip that leads on to Bantry where you can swim. Two minutes' walk to a Restaurant and bar.\r\n\r\nThe Accommodation comprises a hall, kitchen/dining room, lounge, three bedrooms to the first floor and family bathroom.\r\n\r\nCastletownbere is a vibrant fishing town with a selection of restaurants and pubs and a good size supermarket where you can buy local produce. Secondary and primary schools ,churches are also there.\r\n\r\nGround Floor\r\nHall: 4.8m x 1.85m.Double glazed door. Stairs to first floor\r\nLounge: 4.7m x 2.85m. with Open Fire. Window to front aspect. Radiator.\r\nKitchen/Dining: 4.7m x 2.65m with Multi fuel stove with back boiler. Window to front aspect. Range of base units and shelves. Inset stainless sink\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding: Radiator\r\nBedroom: 1. 3.4m x 2.65m. Window to front aspect\r\nBedroom 2- 4.8m x 2.85m. Windows to front and rear aspect\r\nBedroom 3. 2.55m x 2.15m Window to front aspect\r\nBathroom- 2.65m x 1.45m. Window to rear aspect. LLWC. Panelled bath. Wash Hand Basin\r\n\r\nGeneral Disclaimer / Important Notice\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
